# PROJECT: OFFLINESYNC

## Design and Development of a Reusable Offline-First Mobile Data Synchronization Framework with Conflict Resolution

Act as a senior full-stack engineer, distributed systems architect, mobile computing researcher, and software testing engineer.

Build a complete, runnable software project named **OfflineSync**, demonstrated through a realistic e-commerce application called **OfflineShop**.

This is not merely an e-commerce website. The primary contribution is a reusable offline-first synchronization framework. OfflineShop is the end-user application used to demonstrate the framework. A separate OfflineSync Monitor dashboard must expose and visualize the framework's internal synchronization behavior.

I want a functional implementation, not just a design, mockup, code snippets, or a project plan.

---

# 1. PROJECT VISION

Develop a reusable synchronization framework that allows applications to continue operating when network connectivity is unavailable.

The demonstration application will be an e-commerce application where a user can:

- Browse locally cached products.
- Search cached products.
- View product details.
- Add products to a cart.
- Update cart quantities.
- Remove products.
- Add items to a wishlist.
- Select cached addresses.
- Prepare checkout.
- Create an offline order intent.
- View local order history.
- Continue working while offline.

When network connectivity returns, OfflineSync must synchronize queued operations with the backend.

The system must detect, handle and record synchronization failures, duplicate operations, interrupted synchronization and conflicts.

The framework must be designed so that it can eventually be reused in other applications and ported to Android.

