# 5. OFFLINE-FIRST REQUIREMENTS

Offline-first behavior must be genuine.

The application must not simply display an offline toggle while continuing to depend on the server.

The local database must support:

- Cached product catalogue.
- Cached product details.
- Cached categories.
- Local cart.
- Local wishlist.
- Local checkout information.
- Local order intents.
- Local operation queue.
- Sync metadata.
- Cached server records.
- Local activity history.

The frontend should prioritize local reads.

Whenever possible:

1. Read from IndexedDB.
2. Display data immediately.
3. Synchronize in the background.
4. Update the local database with server changes.
5. Update UI state.

When offline:

- Product browsing must use cached products.
- Cart operations must work.
- Wishlist operations must work.
- Checkout preparation must work.
- Order intent creation must work.
- Operations must persist across refreshes.
- The user must not lose locally created data.

Implement network connectivity detection.

Do not rely solely on navigator.onLine for determining whether synchronization requests actually work.

Handle failed requests even when the browser reports online.

