Operation statuses:

- PENDING.
- PROCESSING.
- ACKNOWLEDGED.
- FAILED.
- REQUIRES_ACTION.

Operations must persist across page refreshes and browser restarts.

Implement:

- Unique operation IDs.
- Operation ordering where required.
- Batch synchronization.
- Retry.
- Retry backoff.
- Idempotent processing.
- Acknowledgement.
- Failure handling.
- Operation dependencies where required.
- Recovery from interrupted synchronization.

Do not remove an operation from the local queue until the backend confirms its outcome.

Handle duplicate operation delivery safely.

The backend must be able to receive the same operation more than once without creating duplicate business records.

Use MongoDB unique indexes for idempotency where appropriate.

